`FragCanvas` owns one runtime loop, scheduler, WebGPU renderer, canvas element, and adapter context.

## Import

<FrameworkBlock
svelteCode={`import { FragCanvas } from 'spektral/svelte';`}
reactCode={`import { FragCanvas } from 'spektral/react';`}
vueCode={`import { FragCanvas } from 'spektral/vue';`}
svelteLang="ts"
reactLang="ts"
vueLang="ts"
/>

## Rendering props

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `material` | `FragMaterial` | Required |
| `clearColor` | RGBA tuple | `[0, 0, 0, 1]` |
| `passes` | `AnyPass[]` | `[]` |
| `renderTargets` | `RenderTargetDefinitionMap` | `{}` |
| `renderMode` | `'always' &#124; 'on-demand' &#124; 'manual'` | `'always'` |
| `autoRender` | `boolean` | `true` |
| `maxDelta` | `number` | `0.1` seconds |
| `dpr` | `number` | `devicePixelRatio`, or `1` during SSR |

`material` must come from `defineMaterial(...)`. `maxDelta` must be finite and greater than zero. `passes` may mix pre-scene compute/feedback passes and post-scene render passes.

## Color pipeline

`color` configures final presentation. Changing it recreates the renderer.

| Option | Default | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `outputEncoding` | `'srgb'` | Linear-to-sRGB encoding; `'linear'` leaves values unchanged |
| `toneMapping` | `'none'` | Optional built-in HDR-to-SDR tone mapper |
| `dynamicRange` | `'sdr'` | `'hdr'` requests extended `rgba16float`; `'auto'` falls back to SDR |
| `canvasColorSpace` | `'srgb'` | Canvas presentation space, including optional `'display-p3'` |
| `workingFormat` | `'auto'` | Uses `rgba16float` for HDR or tone mapping; otherwise canvas format |

`ToneMapping`, `OutputDynamicRange`, `CanvasColorSpace`, and `ColorPipelineOptions` are exported
from the root, core, and framework adapter entrypoints.

Available `toneMapping` values:

| Value | Algorithm |
| --- | --- |
| `'none'` | No tone curve |
| `'khronos-pbr-neutral'` | Khronos PBR Neutral |
| `'uncharted2-filmic'` | Uncharted 2 / Hable Filmic with the reference `2.0` exposure bias and `11.2` white point |
| `'aces-hill'` | Stephen Hill's ACES RRT and ODT fit, including its input and output color transforms |
| `'gran-turismo'` | Hajime Uchimura's 2017 Gran Turismo triple-section curve with its published defaults |

All built-in tone mappers expect non-negative linear scene color and produce SDR output. Tone mapping and explicit HDR output cannot be enabled together. Render passes execute before the private presentation pass.

Material and pass shaders return straight alpha. Final canvas presentation premultiplies the output.

## WebGPU configuration

| Prop | Forwarded to |
| --- | --- |
| `adapterOptions` | `navigator.gpu.requestAdapter(...)` |
| `deviceDescriptor` | `adapter.requestDevice(...)` |

Value changes recreate the renderer and its owned device.

## Error handling

| Prop | Default | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `showErrorOverlay` | `true` | Enables default or custom error UI |
| `errorRenderer` | — | Svelte snippet or React callback replacing default UI |
| Vue `#errorRenderer` | — | Scoped slot receiving `{ report }` |
| `onError` | — | Receives every normalized report regardless of overlay state |
| `errorHistoryLimit` | `0` | Enables deduplicated bounded history when positive |
| `onErrorHistory` | — | Receives fresh history arrays |

See [Error Handling](/docs/error-handling) for report codes, source mapping, history semantics, retries, and device errors.

## Canvas, attributes, and children

Native canvas attributes are forwarded to the internal `<canvas>`, except `width`, `height`, `color`, and Spektral prop names. Use `class` in Svelte/Vue, `className` in React, and each framework's native `style` form.

Spektral controls backing-store `width` and `height` from measured CSS size and DPR. The canvas fills its private wrapper; wrap `FragCanvas` when container-level layout is required.

Access the canvas with Svelte `bind:canvas`, the React 19 `ref` prop, or a Vue component ref exposing `canvas` and `getCanvas()`.

Children render inside the Spektral context. Use a Svelte snippet, React children, or Vue default slot for components calling runtime hooks.

## Lifecycle

- Mount creates contexts and the registry, starts the runtime loop, and initializes the renderer asynchronously.
- Pipeline-signature changes destroy the old renderer before recreation.
- Unmount stops the loop, destroys renderer resources and the device, and clears the registry.
